# General principles — one subdirectory chapter per principle (pointer array below,
# populated as the subchapters land).
!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
General principles
description: the small set of rules everything else in the language follows from
- >
  yamlover is built on a handful of principles, each simple to state and far-reaching in consequence.
  Every later part of this spec — the model, the concretes, the pointer and query grammar — is an
  elaboration of the rules on this page; when two readings of a construct compete, the one that keeps
  these principles wins.
- *: order-is-data
- *: one-node
- *: keys-are-pointers
- *: graph-not-tree
- *: names-not-fetches
- *: many-concretes
- *: metadata-first
- *: tolerance
- *: losslessness
